/* Not `#include <streambu>`: Watcom's own streambuf header cannot be included
on its own.  It uses streampos and streamoff (streambu lines 92, 95, 114, 119)
without defining them or including anything that does, and the result is twenty
errors inside the compiler's own header.  <fstream> is self-contained, pulls
streambuf in correctly, and is what a program that wants std::streambuf can be
given.  Measured: <fstream>, <sstream>, <iostream> and <iomanip> all compile on
their own; <streambuf> alone does not.

So this forwarder deliberately offers more than its name suggests, which is
cheaper than the alternative of patching the compiler's headers.
*/
#include <fstream>
